      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-02-06T12:26:47.000Z",
      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues miss analyst expectations",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹1.61 (down from ₹3.86 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹17.8b (up 9.2% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹274.0m (down 58% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 1.5% (down from 4.0% in 3Q 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.6%. Earnings per share (EPS) also missed analyst estimates by 69%. Revenue is forecast to grow 7.5% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 9.3% growth forecast for the Forestry industry in Asia. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 45% per year but the company’s share price has only fallen by 6% per year, which means it has not declined as severely as earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
